+# AI log — SCRUM-252 (US31 · F-100 demo scenarios: fuse, voltage, phase) — 2026-11-15
+
+**Author:** Yeison Delgado · **Tool:** Claude (Claude Code)
+
+## What the AI generated
+- `backend/src/scenarios/`: `GET /scenarios` (demo mode and the actions) and `POST /scenarios`
+  (OPEN_FUSE, CLOSE_FUSE, CUT_VOLTAGE, RESTORE_VOLTAGE, DROP_PHASE, RESTORE_PHASE), with Swagger DTOs.
+- `scenario-actions.ts`: one registry with what each action writes, so SCRUM-253 can add its actions there.
+- Unit tests for the actions, the service and the controller; e2e test `test/scenarios.e2e-spec.ts` over HTTP.
+- `DEMO_SCENARIOS_ENABLED`: `.env.example` (false), local `docker-compose.yml` (true), Render staging (true),
+  Render production (false).
+
+## What I did / reviewed
+- A scenario writes what the device would send: one telemetry reading and one alarm event with the
+  Technical Annex §4.2 code (13xx20, 13xx21, 05xx21y), SET or CLEAR. Nothing in the state or fault logic
+  changes, so the map, the alarm list and the node detail react through their normal rules.
+- Safety (NF-03): off unless `DEMO_SCENARIOS_ENABLED=true`; only Colbits administrators; scope applied;
+  a repeated action (opening an open fuse) is refused with 409 so SET/CLEAR pairs stay consistent;
+  a phase the transformer does not have is refused (CL-07).
+- Ran: 729 unit tests, lint, build, Prettier; e2e on PostgreSQL with Colbits' triggers (176 + 3, 6 new):
+  OPEN_FUSE → node CRITICAL + FUSE_OPENING fault, CLOSE_FUSE → NORMAL and no fault, CUT_VOLTAGE → WARNING +
+  NO_VOLTAGE, one dropped phase → WARNING, two → CRITICAL + two PHASE_LOSS, restores → NORMAL; 403 for a
+  consultation user, 404, 400, 401. Duplication check: 0 clones.
